# Milestone 29: preformatted text and code (reference/common/text-formatting.md and reference/components/markdown.md).
# Page of 200 × 300 with margins of 20: page area of 160 × 260 from (20, 20). Lines of 12 (Size 10); with the test
# metrics each character measures 5 pt.
#   term:    Preformatted pre, five lines of the block, the fourth empty (a blank line is a line,
#            it does not separate paragraphs), and a tab after "PE" that leads to column 4. The longest one is
#            18 characters, 90 pt: it fits and is not broken. 5 × 12 = 60. y = 20.
#   tabs:    Tab size 8: "a" + tab is 8 columns and "abcdefgh" + tab, 16; two lines: 24. y = 80.
#   wrapped: pre-wrap. The first line of the text, "  aaaa bbbb cccc dddd eeee ffff gggg hhhh" (42
#            characters), breaks after "ffff": the indent is kept and the words up to "ffff" are 31
#            characters, 155 pt (with " gggg" they would be 36 characters, 180). "gggg hhhh" remains, and the
#            second line of the text, "corta": 3 lines, 36. y = 104.
#   plain:   without Preformatted, the spaces are collapsed: one line of 12. y = 140.
#   md:      a Markdown with Code font: a one-line Paragraph ("Usa ls -l aquí." with "ls -l" in the code
#            font; in a paragraph the spaces are collapsed, also in inline code: 12) and a
#            two-line code block ("a  b" and "  c"), which is a Text with Preformatted pre: 24.
#            The two follow each other without margins: 36. y = 152.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 200
		Height: 300
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Mono
				Size: 10
	Section:
		Text:
			Id: term
			Typography:
				Preformatted: true
			Content >>
				> Ajustes > Bornes
				L   230 V   [ OK ]
				N     0 V   [ OK ]

				PE	tierra
		Text:
			Id: tabs
			Typography:
				Preformatted: true
				Tab size: 8
			Content >>
				a	b
				abcdefgh	x
		Text:
			Id: wrapped
			Typography:
				Preformatted: wrap
			Content >>
				  aaaa bbbb cccc dddd eeee ffff gggg hhhh
				corta
		Text: a   b    c
			Id: plain
		Markdown:
			Id: md
			Typography:
				Code font: IBM Plex Mono
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
			Content >>
				Usa `ls  -l` aquí.

				```
				a  b
				  c
				```
